meta {
  name: Write under a correlation identifier
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

patch {
  url: {{host}}/books/{{bookId}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-Correlation-Id: {{correlationId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "author": "Martin Fowler, with Kent Beck"
  }
}

docs {
  200. Sets up the request below by making a change under a correlation identifier we choose.

  The API echoes X-Correlation-Id on every response and stamps it on every entry the request
  produces, so supplying one here means the next request can pull the whole thing back out.

  A PATCH rather than a create, deliberately: it can be run repeatedly. A create would answer
  409 on the second run, and a refused request writes no audit entry - so the trace would come
  back empty and look like a broken filter when it is actually the trail correctly recording
  that nothing happened.

  Needs Books > Create a book to have run first, for bookId.
}
